*   **Description:**  Enucleation of the cyst followed by curettage (scraping) of the cyst cavity and placement of a bone graft (typically allograft - donor bone from another source).
*   **Rationale:** The bone graft is intended to fill the cavity and provide a scaffold for new bone formation, theoretically reducing recurrence.
