**Important Note:**  It's important to note that the ""sulfur heads"" may not always be readily visible on routine microscopic examination of the pus.  Special stains (like Hematoxylin and Eosin - H&E) and cultures are often needed for definitive diagnosis.  Sometimes, the organisms are obscured by the dense inflammatory reaction.

