    *   **Projection to Sympathetic Nucleus (Dorsal Ventral Nucleus):** The MNS also projects to the dorsal ventral nucleus (DVN), which is part of the sympathetic nervous system.  Increased activity in the MTS leads to *decreased* sympathetic outflow.  This means less sympathetic stimulation of the heart (less increase in heart rate and contractility) and blood vessels (",ground_truth_similarity,"# Task Description
