No, radiographic evidence alone is insufficient to diagnose extranodal extension (ENE). Clinical examination findings, such as skin involvement, tethering to adjacent structures, or cranial nerve deficits, are required for a definitive diagnosis. Radiographic findings should support, but not replace, physical exam findings.  

\boxed{No}
