| Coordination Sites | Histidine, Water, Amino Acids (e.ry. Glutamate) | Stabilizes the metal, provides a suitable environment for the reaction |

**In summary:** The 6-coordinate coordination sphere of the zinc ion in carbonic anhydrase is not just a structural feature; it's a critical component of the catalytic mechanism. It stabilizes the water molecule, enhances its acidity, facilitates protonation, and facilitates the overall reaction of CO₂ to bicarbonate.",relevance,"# Task Description
