To find $z$, we divide both sides by $3 + \sqrt{3}i$:
$$z = \frac{-2\sqrt{3}i}{3 + \sqrt{3}i}$$
To simplify this, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, which is $3 - \sqrt{3}i$:
$$z = \frac{-2\sqrt{3}i}{3 + \sqrt{3}i} \cdot \frac{3 - \sqrt{3}i}{3 - \sqrt{3}i} = \frac{-2\sqrt{3}i(3 - \sqrt{3}i}}{3^2 + (\sqrt{3})^2} = \frac{-6\sqrt{3}i + 2\sqrt{3}i^2}{9 + 3} = \frac{-6\sqrt{3}i - 2\sqrt{3}}{12} = \frac{-2\sqrt{3}}{12} - \frac{6\sqrt{3}}{12}i = \frac{-1}{6}\sqrt{3} - \frac{1}{2}\sqrt{3}i$$
