$I = \frac{1}{12} b t^3$

Now, substitute this value of $I$ into the formula for the deflection:

$$ \delta_{=} = \frac{P L^3}{6 \pi E \left \frac{1}{1} \frac{1}{12} b t^3 \right} = \frac{P L^3}{6 \pi E \frac{1}{12} b t^3} = \frac{12 \pi}{12} \frac{P L^3}{E b t^3} = \frac{2 \pi L^3}{E b t^3} $$

Therefore, the maximum deflection of the triangular-shaped cantilever beam is:

