**1. Measurement Error (Detector and Detector Electronics)**

*   **Detector Resolution:** Any detector used to detect the decay products of the Σ⁺ (typically a positron and a proton) will have a finite resolution. This means the energy of the detected particles will not be precisely measured, but will be spread around the true energy. The amount of spread is the detector's resolution.
*   **Detector Electronics Noise:** The electronics used to read the detector signal also have a certain level of noise, which introduces another source of uncertainty.
*   **Detector Calibration:**  Calibration of the detector is crucial.  Errors in calibration will directly affect the measured energy.

