*   **Quantum Fluctuations:**  Unlike classical optimization methods that might get trapped in local minima (local ""dips"" in the hill), quantum annealing uses quantum fluctuations (quantum tunneling) to explore the landscape more broadly.  This increases the chance of finding the global minimum (the very lowest point).
